DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The cclloocckk__ggeettccppuucclloocckkiidd() function obtains the ID of the CPU‐time clock
       of the process whose ID is _p_i_d, and returns it in the location pointed
       to by _c_l_o_c_k_i_d.  If _p_i_d is zero, then the clock ID of the CPU‐time clock
       of the calling process is returned.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, cclloocckk__ggeettccppuucclloocckkiidd() returns 0; on error, it returns one
       of the positive error numbers listed in ERRORS.

EERRRROORRSS
       EENNOOSSYYSS The  kernel  does not support obtaining the per‐process CPU‐time
              clock of another process, and _p_i_d does not specify  the  calling
              process.

       EEPPEERRMM  The caller does not have permission to access the CPU‐time clock
              of  the  process  specified by _p_i_d.  (Specified in POSIX.1‐2001;
              does not occur on Linux unless the kernel does not  support  ob‐
              taining the per‐process CPU‐time clock of another process.)

       EESSRRCCHH  There is no process with the ID _p_i_d.

